---URI Override. When specified, all the HTTP tasks inside the queue will be partially or fully overridden depending on the configured values.
---@class gcp.cloudtasks_v2.UriOverride
---@field host? string Host override. When specified, replaces the host part of the task URL. For example, if the task URL is "https://www.google.com," and host value is set to "example.net", the overridden URI will be changed to "https://example.net." Host value cannot be an empty string (INVALID_ARGUMENT).
---@field uriOverrideEnforceMode? gcp.cloudtasks_v2.UriOverrideUriOverrideEnforceModeEnum|string URI Override Enforce Mode When specified, determines the Target UriOverride mode. If not specified, it defaults to ALWAYS.
---@field scheme? gcp.cloudtasks_v2.UriOverrideSchemeEnum|string Scheme override. When specified, the task URI scheme is replaced by the provided value (HTTP or HTTPS).
---@field queryOverride? gcp.cloudtasks_v2.QueryOverride URI query. When specified, replaces the query part of the task URI. Setting the query value to an empty string clears the URI query segment.
---@field port? string Port override. When specified, replaces the port part of the task URI. For instance, for a URI "https://www.example.com/example" and port=123, the overridden URI becomes "https://www.example.com:123/example". Note that the port value must be a positive integer. Setting the port to 0 (Zero) clears the URI port.
---@field pathOverride? gcp.cloudtasks_v2.PathOverride URI path. When specified, replaces the existing path of the task URL. Setting the path value to an empty string clears the URI path segment.

